   keeps chunk boundaries aligned with the model that creates and verifies the
   stored vectors without initializing an unrelated provider.
 
+- Reranking reports unavailable inference contexts as an error instead of
+  caching neutral fallback scores. Versioned score-cache keys also exclude old
+  fallback, double-sigmoid, and intent-insensitive entries.
+- SDK searches accept `sourceLimit` (default 20) to widen each lexical/vector
+  retrieval independently from the fused `candidateLimit` used for reranking.
+- SDK `update()` preserves expansion and rerank caches, including on no-op
+  updates; changed chunk text naturally receives a new rerank cache key.
+
 ## [2.8.3] - 2026-08-16
 
 ### Security
